      </j:conditional>
      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>This prayer (in two parts) begins with a focus on the difficult people in our lives, then shifts and becomes a prayer that we ourselves not be difficult people in the lives of others.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65785_introduction"/>
      <j:conditional xml:id="osp_65785_notes">
        <tei:fs type="opensiddur:paratext">
          <tei:f name="include">
            <tei:binary value="true"/>
          </tei:f>
        </tei:fs>
      </j:conditional>
      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“A Prayer for Difficult People (in two parts)” was first offered on Yom Kippur 5772 (2011) at Pleasantville Community Synagogue (Pleasantville, NY), and has since appeared in congregational newsletters, blogs, and on the website “Restless Pilgrim.”</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65785_notes"/>
